Vendored third-party crates whose licenses are compatible with AGPL-3.0
(Apache-2.0, MIT, or BSD-3-Clause) are recorded below. The fapico2
firmware as a whole remains AGPL-3.0; the permissive licenses of these
dependencies are one-way compatible into AGPL-3.0 and do not relax any
fapico2 user's rights under the AGPL.

**The AGPL network clause and the emulation binary.** A hardware token
serves no network, so section 13 (Remote Network Interaction) is inert for
the flashed firmware. The emulation binary is different: it serves CCID +
CTAP-HID over TCP sockets. Anyone who offers *that* as a network service
owes its users the corresponding source, exactly as section 13 requires.

